From 77ae529b2b41297ec829de8d7fc84dd764c05ef5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:17:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign Lab Prioritas as a wide workspace with analytical
 charts

Present the LIVE/DEMO Lab as a 1600px decision workspace: settings on the
left (scenario, weights, criteria, scope), analysis on the right in reading
order: weight chart, status, ranking, contribution breakdown, then
expandable sources, method and checks.

- WeightChart shows chosen vs effective weights and stays visible when a
  result is withheld; RankingChart and ContributionChart render only after
  the composite integrity and score-direction checks pass, each with a
  text/table equivalent.
- StatusPanel gives one heading, one sentence and an expandable
  "Lihat alasan dan detail teknis" per state (validated, loading,
  incomplete, blocked, error, DEMO); retry only where it helps.
- Kaca: one translucent settings panel over opaque inner cards, dense
  enough to keep muted text at WCAG AA over the lightest backdrop; solid
  fallbacks for missing backdrop-filter, reduced transparency and high
  contrast; reduced motion respected.
- FeaturePageFrame gains an optional workspace max-width (default 1760px
  unchanged). RankingResults is replaced by AnalysisPanel, LabCharts,
  LabDetails and StatusPanel.

Integrity guards, LIVE/DEMO isolation, direction checks, source
attribution and the original/effective weight disclosure are unchanged.

